# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and the working tree on every
# platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true. Without this file, a Windows
# contributor's commits can land CRLF in the stored blobs -- which is exactly
# what happened during the Windows bring-up: `src/turmeric_script.cpp` went from
# 0 CR bytes upstream to 457 in a single commit, invisibly, because the diff
# still reads cleanly on the machine that made it. Everyone else then sees a
# whole-file rewrite on the next touch.
#
# It also matters for correctness, not just diff hygiene: the `.tur` scripts
# under examples/ are fed to the Turmeric reader, and the compiler copies
# inline-C block bodies VERBATIM into generated C. Stray \r bytes ride along.
# The compiler repo pins eol=lf for that reason; this repo should match.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.svg    text
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.wav    binary
*.ogg    binary
*.mp3    binary

# Build artifacts. Normally gitignored, but marked so a stray `git add -f`
# cannot corrupt one.
*.dll    binary
*.so     binary
*.dylib  binary
*.a      binary
*.o      binary
*.obj    binary
*.exe    binary
*.lib    binary
